messages:
emily: Quick sync — I'm starting the migration of the Troubleshooting & Error Reference doc (429s, timeouts, context limits, fallback behaviour) into the new 'error-ref' layout. Need: 1) owners for each subsection, 2) updated SDK fallback snippets, 3) link sanity-checks. I dropped a rough checklist in the PR description: https://git.redwood/infra/docs/pulls/4321 :wave:

ben: I can own the SDK snippets section. Do we want to consolidate the JS + Python fallback examples into a single conceptual example, or keep them separate?

emily: thanks ben — prefer consolidated concept + two tiny language snippets. The conceptual example should show: detect 429, exponential backoff with jitter, then an eventual fallback to a smaller model variant or cached response. Keep token trimming mention brief.

ben: ok. Quick sketch for JS fallback snippet — wdyt?

ben: ```js
// detect 429, backoff, fallback to cached summary or smaller model
async function requestWithFallback(client, req) {
  try {
    return await client.generate(req)
  } catch (err) {
    if (err.status === 429) {
      await backoffWithJitter()
      // try smaller model
      req.model = 'small-llm-v1'
      return await client.generate(req)
    }
    throw err
  }
}
```

leah: This is good. For the docs UX we should also add a tiny flow diagram (sequence) and two bullets under "When to fallback" — cost vs latency vs output-quality tradeoffs. I can add the diagram.

sam: Heads-up — the current error-ref cross-links still point to the old examples folder; I'll open a small PR to redirect them after the main doc lands. Also we should add a note about long-running streaming responses hitting context window limits and recommended server-side trimming.

emily: yes, add the trimming note. Use this suggested phrasing: "If responses exceed the model's context window, prefer server-side prefix trimming or summarize-and-append to preserve salient context." Keep it 1-2 sentences.

ben: one question on tests — do we want unit-level snippets in the repo that the docs reference? Or rely on manual smoke tests?

leah: put minimal unit/snippet tests in tests/docs-snippets/. They can be very small and run in CI; I'll add a pytest for the python snippet and a tiny node test for JS.

deploy-bot: lint-check: docs/snippets/js/fallback.js failed (line 12) — trailing whitespace.

ben: whoops will fix.

emily: timeline: target to merge main doc PR by Wed EOD, follow-ups (tests, redirects, diagram) by next Fri. If anyone needs more time, call it out here.

sam: I'm out Wed morning — can review Wed afternoon.

leah: fine to land core text without diagram, I'll PR diagram next day.

ben: fixed trailing whitespace, pushed a tiny test. PR: https://git.redwood/infra/docs/pulls/4322 — tagged @emily @leah @sam for review.

emily: awesome. After merge I'll run a quick sweep for broken links and then coordinate the SDK snippets release. :tada:
